WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.502
In this video, you will plan a whole evening of lights.

00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.596
You will save the places you like, put them in a sensible driving order, and send the route to your maps app.

00:00:09.596 --> 00:00:10.704
We start on the map.

00:00:11.605 --> 00:00:13.354
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:16.135 --> 00:00:18.652
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.501
Then tap Allow.

00:00:25.476 --> 00:00:26.576
Let's plan a night.

00:00:26.576 --> 00:00:28.555
First, choose what you want to see.

00:00:28.555 --> 00:00:29.764
Tap the season button.

00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:33.045
Pick the one you want.

00:00:33.045 --> 00:00:37.127
Christmas lights are the biggest, so tap Thanksgiving and Christmas Lights.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:42.245
Halloween, New Year, and other seasons are in the same list.

00:00:43.145 --> 00:00:46.367
When you see a place you want to visit, tap the heart on its card.

00:00:48.596 --> 00:00:50.523
That saves it to your favorites.

00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:51.166
Add a few.

00:00:51.166 --> 00:00:52.159
I will add three.

00:00:53.058 --> 00:00:55.106
Now tap the heart tab, Favorites.

00:00:56.914 --> 00:00:58.787
Your hearts are collected here.

00:00:58.787 --> 00:01:06.045
The stops are put in a sensible driving order, with the miles and the time they add up to, so you do not zigzag across town.

00:01:06.944 --> 00:01:10.013
You can choose where to start, and which maps app to use.

00:01:10.013 --> 00:01:12.235
When you are ready to go, tap Route these.

00:01:14.121 --> 00:01:20.602
Your maps app takes about nine stops at a time, so a long night is split into routes of nine or fewer.

00:01:20.602 --> 00:01:23.371
Each route starts where the last one ended.

00:01:23.371 --> 00:01:26.580
A route with nine stops or fewer is a single route.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:30.332
As you go, tick each stop when you have been there.

00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:36.311
That way, if you stop for dinner, or save the rest for another night, you can see exactly where you left off.

00:01:38.039 --> 00:01:43.588
Each route has its own button, and it opens in your maps app, ready for turn by turn directions.

00:01:43.588 --> 00:01:49.939
You can choose Apple Maps, Google Maps, or Waze, and the change button next to Opens in switches between them.

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:53.886
On a phone, the site asks the first time, and remembers your choice.

00:01:53.886 --> 00:01:57.605
Waze takes one stop at a time, so it starts with the first stop.

00:01:57.605 --> 00:02:00.580
Phones also show a Send to car button on each stop.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:01.953
Then tap the X to close.

00:02:03.631 --> 00:02:05.372
Planning with family or friends?

00:02:05.372 --> 00:02:07.535
Tap Share to send your favorites to them.

00:02:09.953 --> 00:02:14.198
They can open the same list on their own phone, and add it to their own favorites.

00:02:15.098 --> 00:02:17.119
Tap the heart on places you like.

00:02:17.119 --> 00:02:23.063
Route these splits your night into routes of nine or fewer, each starting where the last one ended.

00:02:23.063 --> 00:02:24.549
Tick off stops as you go.

00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:27.933
Next up: Weekly lights email.
